%description:

Tcp.keepAliveIdleTime:invalid -- a negative value stops the run with an error at the open.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the idle time before the first keepalive probe (RFC 9293 MUST-28: at
least two hours; Linux tcp_keepalive_time); 0 or more".

The classes: rfc (7200 s, the default), other (another value) and invalid (a negative value).
The code: TcpAlgorithmBase::initializeAlgorithm() reads the value at the open of each connection
and stops the run for a negative value, which would else reach the scheduler, also when
keepalive is off. This test separates "invalid" from the other classes.

Host under test: host1, with the value -1s; host1 opens a connection to host2 at 0.1 s. Observation:
level 0, the run stops at the open of the connection with the error of the check.

%# parameter: Tcp.keepAliveIdleTime
%# class: invalid
%# value: -1s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.keepAliveIdleTime
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpKeepAliveIdleTimeInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveIdleTime = -1s    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
keepAliveIdleTime must be 0 or more, but it is -1
